<!--
  Connection graph viewer v4 -- the acquaintance map.

  What this shows: every person you have a live connection to, as a dot on a 2D map you pan and zoom.
  Position means shared context: people who share group chats and who the data implies know each other are pulled together, so the canvas reads as social regions (family, work, a college thread) rather than as a hierarchy ranked around you.
  You are implicit -- there is no center node, no rings, no "closeness tier".
  Group chats are never drawn as map objects; they exist only as invisible layout anchors and as evidence you can inspect (the groups drawer, or a person's connection panel).
